217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (The city is synthetic and generated from a seed \(42 in all runs\), so every machine builds the same city. It has 38 nodes: Traffic 11, Water 9, Power 9, Air Quality 8 and Emergency 7. Six nodes belong to two domains at once, for example a pumping station that depends on power, so the domain counts add up to 44. The nodes are distributed over 6 zones and connected by 10 roads and 67 links. A link joins two neighbouring nodes, so a layer can query what lies next to a node. A sixth layer, Land, has no nodes and serves as the base map.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (Each node has a fixed GPS position \(anchor 36.0 N, 10.0 E, one map unit equals 5 m, which makes the city about 9.6 km by 5.4 km\). The city, its streets and its coordinates are invented and do not represent real data.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
