327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1099 0 R
/E (One key per caller. Keys are compared in constant time and kept out of the repository. The Twin refuses to start if a key is missing, too short or identical to another key.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/E (A gate in front of every action. actuate runs its checks in a fixed order: the request is well formed, the idempotency key, the token, the dry run where one is required, and the cap. Without a valid token no action is executed.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1101 0 R
/E (Tokens. The Twin has two modes. Unsigned mode accepts the team's own test token. Signed mode verifies the Guardian's g1 token \(Ed25519\). In both modes the Twin rejects a token that has expired, has already been used, belongs to another run, names a different action or key, has a lifetime over 60 seconds, or carries a score outside 0 to 1 \(including NaN\). A token is only marked as used when the action commits.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1102 0 R
/E (Exactly-once execution. A repeated request with the same idempotency key returns the first answer. The same key with a changed request is rejected.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1103 0 R
/E (Fail-safe behaviour. With Redis enabled, actuate refuses and changes nothing when Redis cannot be reached \(STATE_UNAVAILABLE\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1104 0 R
/E (Containment restricted to the Guardian. An actuate aimed at a node with a held device is refused \(DEVICE_QUARANTINED\) and the command is kept for the Guardian to read.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
