/T (Role and goals)
/E (Role and goals)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
439 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (The Guardian checks whether sensor evidence is trustworthy and whether a proposed action meets the agreed policy. It receives readings from the Twin, scores them using deterministic validation and reputation rules, and provides the Brain with trust verdicts and action authorization. It does not choose or execute city actions. The Brain plans; the Twin decides whether a command is valid and changes the simulated city.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
440 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (The Guardian also handles containment. It delegates isolation, quarantine, rollback and release to the Twin. After the Twin confirms an effect, the Guardian mirrors that state for its own scoring and notifies the Brain. Its main goals are to keep evidence traceable to its readings, refuse actions that do not meet policy, and keep the authorization decision separate from the final execution gate in the Twin.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 110 0 R
/T (Architecture)
/E (Architecture)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
442 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (Twin readings enter the Guardian through the Bearer-authenticated SSE feed and are normalized into the Guardian's reading model. The Guardian checks reading structure, units, ordering and duplicate delivery before scoring. Conflicting content under an existing reading ID is rejected; skipped tick gaps are recorded.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
443 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (The scoring service applies deterministic validation, correlation and reputation checks. The Random Forest model may add an advisory, but its output has zero numeric weight in the trust score. Current trust states are Trusted at 0.7 or higher, Degraded above 0.3 and below 0.7, and Untrusted at 0.3 or lower.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
444 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (For authorization, the Guardian checks the current verdict and its supporting reading IDs, the action's domain and risk, the exact parameters and targets, and the Twin's discovered action and containment state. If the checks pass, the Guardian signs a g1 action token with Ed25519. The Twin verifies the token and remains responsible for enforcing its action limits and executing the command.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
445 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (15/20)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
446 0 obj
<<
