/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
469 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (Each service link uses its own Bearer credential. The Twin feed is Bearer-authenticated; it does not carry signed readings in twin-mock-3. This is separate from the Guardian's Ed25519 g1 signature on action tokens, which the Twin verifies with the Guardian's configured public key.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
470 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (Token claims bind the run, action, targets, parameters, idempotency key, supporting reading IDs and key ID. Tokens use Twin-simulated time and are limited to 60 simulated seconds; the Twin enforces one-time use when it accepts a command. If Twin discovery or the required signing key is unavailable, the Guardian fails closed.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
471 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (Reading-signature requirements are controlled by the Guardian's configuration, not by a caller-supplied per-reading switch. Any signature that is supplied is validated. Demo mode bypasses authentication on protected routes and is intended only for local demonstrations; it is off by default.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
472 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (The Guardian records reading evaluations, authorization decisions and containment outcomes in JSON Lines audit logs. It does not put full action tokens in those logs.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
